# Dogfood history and scope

- Before proposing test work or reporting what remains, read the relevant
  existing run reports under `docs/dogfood/runs/`, commit history, and the
  user's latest scope corrections. Missing evidence in a new ledger is not
  evidence that historical testing never happened.
- Preserve completed baseline work and existing in-progress changes. Keep
  historical passes, current-candidate passes, observed regressions, and
  genuinely untested cases separate. Reopen a completed area only for a
  specific observed regression or an explicitly requested new qualification.
- Jon confirmed on October 7, 2026 that sign-in/account switching, repository
  switching, integrations, billing, autocomplete, editing, and reload testing
  were already completed. The active repair is file selection -> body read ->
  source retention -> grounded answer/citation. See
  `docs/dogfood/runs/2026-10-07-file-context/README.md` for its evidence ledger.
- Do not say “we still need to test billing/sign-in” because this file-context
  candidate has no new billing/sign-in entry. Say “the historical baseline
  remains completed; this candidate's closed-file read still needs a replay.”
- Follow `ship-claim-discipline.mdc`: automated green is not a live Pass. A
  completion report must name actual live results and any remaining gaps in
  plain language; do not silently stop after tests or a build.
